---Cancel a run
---
---Cancels a run that has not finished — queued or running — and returns it. Canceling a finished run changes nothing and returns it as it ended. The runner releases any sandbox the run allocated, including one whose provisioning was in flight. Project read access admits the caller; anyone else reads the project as not found. A repository's readers act through its own run routes (/repos/{repo_id}/runs). Requires push on the repository (automation principals also project write or manage), and canManageAgents to cancel a run someone else started or a push started. Served only by the project's primary processing cell.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/runs/{id}/cancel`
---@param input entire.runs.CancelProjectRunRequest
---@return entire.runs.Run? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_project_run(input) end

---Cancel a repository's run
---
---Cancels one of the repository's runs, as POST /{host}/{project}/runs/{id}/cancel does. Requires pull on the repository, and push to start, retry or cancel; nothing of the project that owns it. billing_subject is returned only to the project's readers, events and diagnostic only with push or canManageAgents, and the agent's configuration only with canManageAgents.
---
---`POST /api/v1/repos/{repo_id}/runs/{id}/cancel`
---@param input entire.runs.CancelRepoRunRequest
---@return entire.runs.Run? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_repo_run(input) end

---Run an agent
---
---Starts one run of the agent on one of a Trail's Changes, in the Change's repository, which the agent must select: it pins the agent's current version (for a preset agent, the preset as it is now), its Environment and the Change's commits into an immutable snapshot, and queues it for the worker. A paused agent still runs when asked to by a caller with canManageAgents. Idempotency-Key is required: an identical repeat returns the first run even after the agent was edited or archived. Project read access admits the caller; anyone else reads the project as not found. A repository's readers act through its own run routes (/repos/{repo_id}/runs). Requires push on the repository (automation principals also project write or manage); without canManageAgents only an enabled agent runs. Served only by the project's primary processing cell.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}/runs`
---@param input entire.runs.CreateProjectAgentRunRequest
---@return entire.runs.Run? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_project_agent_run(input) end

---Run an agent on a repository's Change
---
