---Get a run
---
---Returns a run's status, the agent, environment, target and runtime it pinned, its provenance, dispatch state, result, captured output, credential-redacted failure diagnostic and events. Events are empty and diagnostic null for a caller without push on the repository or canManageAgents: both are raw process output, redacted only on a best-effort basis. Project read access, or pull on any repository the project owns, admits the caller; anyone else reads the project as not found. Requires pull on the run's repository; events and diagnostic are returned only with push on it or canManageAgents, and billing_subject only to project readers. Served only by the project's primary processing cell.
---
---`GET /api/v1/{host}/{project}/runs/{id}`
---@param input entire.runs.GetProjectRunRequest
---@return entire.runs.Run? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_project_run(input) end

---Get a run's snapshot
---
---Returns the immutable snapshot the run was admitted with: every pinned spec verbatim, the resolved target, rendered prompt, runtime and provenance. It is never re-derived from current configuration, and holds no credential. For a caller without configuration access it holds what the run records of itself, not the agent's configuration: a pinned agent's repository_ids, if present, hold only the run's repository, its instructions and the rendered prompt are left out, and the Environment is its id and version alone. Project read access, or pull on any repository the project owns, admits the caller; anyone else reads the project as not found. Requires pull on the run's repository; events and diagnostic are returned only with push on it or canManageAgents, and billing_subject only to project readers. Served only by the project's primary processing cell.
---
